{"id": "unknown-2026-08-24-026", "date": "2026-08-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Italy’s CNR presents bifacial PV tile based on spectral splitting", "content": "<p>Researchers at Italy’s CNR developed a four-terminal PV tile that uses spectral splitting to direct visible and infrared light to GaAs and bifacial silicon cells, respectively. Outdoor testing confirmed reduced self-shading and enhanced albedo collection, while highlighting opportunities to improve optical efficiency and advance the technology toward commercial applications.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/italys-cnr-presents-bifacial-pv-tile-based-on-spectral-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/italys-cnr-presents-bifacial-pv-tile-based-on-spectral-splitting/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-24-027", "date": "2026-08-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "European PPA prices rise 2.3% in July", "content": "<p>European PPA prices rose 2.3% in July, with gains in Great Britain and Italy offset by declines in the Nordics, Spain and Portugal. Contracting remained active, with 24 PPAs totaling 1.1 GW and nine battery storage agreements representing 865 MW.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/european-ppa-prices-rise-2-3-in-july/\">European PPA prices rise 2.3% in July</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/european-ppa-prices-rise-2-3-in-july/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-24-028", "date": "2026-08-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Korean scientists unveil 10 kW chemical adsorption heat pump prototype", "content": "<p>Korean researchers have developed a 10 kW chemical adsorption heat pump that uses waste heat at around 40 C to provide cooling for buildings, factories and data centers. The prototype features a high-performance adsorption bed, an electrochemical compressor with no moving parts and ammonia as a natural refrigerant.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/korean-scientists-unveil-10-kw-chemical-adsorption-heat-pump-prototype/\">Korean scientists unveil 10 kW chemical ads", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/korean-scientists-unveil-10-kw-chemical-adsorption-heat-pump-prototype/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-24-029", "date": "2026-08-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India hits $0.068/kWh tariff in 4-hour peak renewable power tender", "content": "<p>SECI has discovered a lowest tariff of INR 5.99 ($0.068)/kWh in its 1.5 GW tender for four-hour assured peak renewable power. Waaree Energies secured 700 MW, while NTPC REL and ACME Solar won 500 MW and 300 MW, respectively.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/seci-discovers-inr-5-99-kwh-tariff-for-4-hour-peak-renewable-power/\">India hits $0.068/kWh tariff in 4-hour peak renewable power tender</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/seci-discovers-inr-5-99-kwh-tariff-for-4-hour-peak-renewable-power/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-24-030", "date": "2026-08-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US updates foreign inverter ban to include wired devices", "content": "<p>The FCC expanded its national security Covered List rules to explicitly target Ethernet-connected inverters while creating a compliance pathway for 45X-eligible domestic manufacturing.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/fcc-updates-foreign-inverter-ban-to-include-wired-devices-adds-45x-safe-harbor/\">US updates foreign inverter ban to include wired devices</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/24/fcc-updates-foreign-inverter-ban-to-include-wired-devices-adds-45x-safe-harbor/", "type": "rss"}]}
